Brainstorming & Ideation Phase 
The Brainstorming & Ideation Phase is the stage where different ideas are generated, explored, and discussed to find possible solutions to a problem.
Main steps:
Identify the problem – Clearly understand what needs to be solved.
Generate ideas – Think of as many possible solutions as possible.
Encourage creativity – Avoid judging ideas too early.
Discuss and combine ideas – Improve or merge useful ideas.
Evaluate ideas – Select ideas that are practical and effective.
Choose the best idea – Decide which idea should move forward.
Example:
Problem: Students find it difficult to manage study time.
Ideas: Study timetable app, reminder system, group study, daily planner, or time-management game.
